Subject: [PATCH 35/35] mb/lenovo/haswell: Group the setup menu into categories

The setup menu has three mainboard forms (System, Processor, Graphics)
followed by the four generic H8 forms, and the new CPU, VT-d and iGPU
options are not in it yet. Group everything into five categories, one
form each, split into cards with nested forms:

- General: model, processor, memory, firmware and EC versions (read-only,
  regenerated on every boot), sound, NMI
- Energy Saver: battery, processor power management and power limits,
  cooling policy, USB always-on, power after AC loss
- Security: VT-x, VT-d, Intel ME
- Keyboard: Fn/Ctrl swap, F1-F12 keys, sticky Fn, illumination,
  TrackPoint, touchpad
- Hardware: NVIDIA GPU, iGPU memory and aperture, ExpressCard and
  Thunderbolt (W541), wireless devices

coreboot appends its generic Console form (console log level) to every
CFR menu, so it shows up as a sixth category after these five.

This uses H8_CFR_MAINBOARD_FORMS to place the H8 options. The F1-F12
setting is shown as a list instead of a switch; it uses the same
variable, which holds 0 or 1 either way.

The variables of the existing options do not change.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init, and
checked that the low 16 bits of the CFR object IDs, which EDK2 uses as
question IDs, are unique.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
